        <strong>Profile:</strong> Married couple both 67, receiving $36,000 in annual Social Security benefits. They withdraw $25,000 from an IRA.
      </p>
      <p>
        The $25,000 IRA withdrawal pushes their provisional income from $18,000 to $43,000, causing $11,450 of their Social Security to become taxable. The combined taxable income increases their federal tax from $0 to $1,825.
