        Taking a single $100,000 lump sum in one year pushes $51,525 into the 22% bracket and triggers higher Medicare IRMAA premiums. Spreading the withdrawal as $25,000 per year over four years keeps all dollars inside the 12% bracket, saving over $4,800 in total federal taxes.
